-- title:
--   Flatness descends to a finitely generated subalgebra of the base
-- statement:
--   Let $R_0$, $R$ and $B_0$ be commutative rings with $R$ and $B_0$ given as $R_0$-algebras, and assume that $B_0$ is of finite presentation over $R_0$. Assume further that the base change $R \otimes_{R_0} B_0$ is flat as a module over $R$. Then for every finite subset $s$ of $R$ there is an $R_0$-subalgebra $R_1 \subseteq R$ such that: $R_1$ is finitely generated as an $R_0$-algebra (`Subalgebra.FG`, i.e. generated by a finite subset of $R$); the underlying set of $s$ is contained in $R_1$; and $R_1 \otimes_{R_0} B_0$ is flat as a module over $R_1$. No Noetherian or finiteness hypothesis is imposed on $R_0$ or $R$ themselves, and the flatness obtained at the finite level is global flatness of the $R_1$-module $R_1 \otimes_{R_0} B_0$, not merely flatness after localisation at a prime.
--
--   This is the descent of flatness of a finitely presented algebra to a finite level in the filtered system of finitely generated $R_0$-subalgebras of $R$ (EGA IV, 11.2.6), obtained here from the corresponding statement at a single prime of $R \otimes_{R_0} B_0$ together with the openness of the flat locus over a Noetherian base. It serves in the project as the algebraic input for descending flatness of a pullback to a finite level, and thence for the transfer of finite type and finite presentation along faithfully flat maps.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Module_Flat_exists_fg_subalgebra_flat_tensorProduct.lean

